@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy"; }
<div class="container py-5">
    <div class="surface p-4 p-lg-5">
        <div class="eyebrow">TBA Datalytics Online Learning</div>
        <h1 class="h2 fw-bold mt-2">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-muted-custom">Last updated: October 3, 2026</p>
        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">1. Information we collect</h2>
        <p>We collect information needed to create and operate your account, deliver courses, process enrolment and payments, record assessment progress, review capstone submissions, and issue or verify certificates. This may include your name, email address, account identifiers, course activity, assessment results, and payment references.</p>
        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">2. How we use information</h2>
        <p>We use information to provide learning services, secure accounts, personalise progress views, administer assessments, support instructors, prevent abuse, maintain financial records, and verify certificates.</p>
        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">3. Payment information</h2>
        <p>Payment credentials should be handled by the configured payment provider. The learning platform should retain only the transaction information necessary to reconcile payment and unlock purchased course entitlements.</p>
        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">4. Learning and assessment records</h2>
        <p>Course enrolments, module completion, quiz attempts, capstone reviews, and certificates may be retained as academic and service records.</p>
        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">5. Sharing</h2>
        <p>We do not sell learner data. Information may be shared with service providers where necessary to operate the platform, process payments, host infrastructure, provide security, or comply with legal obligations.</p>
        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">6. Security</h2>
        <p>We use authentication, authorisation, server-side validation, protected storage, and other reasonable technical controls. No internet service can guarantee absolute security.</p>
        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">7. Your choices</h2>
        <p>You may request correction of inaccurate account information and may contact support regarding access, privacy, or deletion requests, subject to records we are legally or operationally required to retain.</p>
        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">8. Policy updates</h2>
        <p>We may update this policy when the platform, services, or legal requirements change. The effective date will be shown above.</p>
    </div>
</div>
